} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473839} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "112fcfe9-f163-5402-bb4c-1c126bca51d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472890} {:answer/id #uuid "448edde1-a526-52c0-ba25-3145d1c46f49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "448edde1-a526-52c0-ba25-3145d1c46f49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472891} :answer-field/id #uuid "db9f241c-836d-5fde-9168-5d59cd8ab428" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473840}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2006d399-9a69-519f-8bb4-45f612aefe6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-213141" :question/problem "Consider the following set:\n\n$$\nA={{0},{0,1}}\n$$\n\nGiven the relation $R$ on $A$ defined by\n\n$$\nX\\,R\\,Y\\,⇔\\,X⊃Y,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** ${0}\\,R\\,{0,1}$\n- **II.** ${0,1}\\,R\\,{0,1}$\n- **III.** ${0}\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,{0}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊂{A}^{2}\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $X\\,R\\,Y$ if and only if $X⊃Y.$ For this relation, note that\n\n- the symbols $R$ and $⊃$ are interchangeable, and\n\n- the symbols $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ and $⊅$ are also interchangeable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $⊃,$ we have ${0}⊃{0,1}.$ This is equivalent to ${0,1}⊂{0},$ which is false.\n\n- Statement II is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $⊃,$ we have ${0,1}⊃{0,1}.$ This is equivalent to ${0,1}⊂{0,1},$ which is false.\n\n- Statement III is true. Replacing $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ with the symbol $⊅,$ we have ${0}⊅{0}.$ This is equivalent to ${0}⊄{0},$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411415 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8479a60b-b5db-5ad4-8100-fd2db8002091" :knowledge-point/title "Using the x R y Notation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050648 :topic/id #uuid "5c32a7e5-b594-532c-868b-817b3d0ee933" :topic/math-academy-id 2817 :topic/title "Relations on Finite Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d941faec-e94f-51c2-a015-6e9922022b3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453700} {:answer/id #uuid "6cf7c851-e652-5e8e-8a5f-aea78dae8d9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6cf7c851-e652-5e8e-8a5f-aea78dae8d9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453701} :answer-field/id #uuid "33241716-9c2f-5527-9caf-28ca41203246" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454600} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d75d6d2-7386-5acc-ad1a-1337eec447d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453702} {:answer/id #uuid "5e5651d3-07d9-555a-b807-433068b6fa9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453703}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d75d6d2-7386-5acc-ad1a-1337eec447d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453702} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb50187f-3fd4-55dd-96b1-59e3e5d83fb4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454601} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9171ea78-358f-5962-92c7-ee1e5b63f94e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453704} {:answer/id #uuid "b1018595-c01c-5712-a26d-4c1d47390d3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453705}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9171ea78-358f-5962-92c7-ee1e5b63f94e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453704} :answer-field/id #uuid "6937c55d-93a2-573c-bbc0-83804147eb3e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454602}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5fbac889-73d0-5b8f-a301-da4ef8cb327a" :question/math-academy-id "q-213127" :question/problem "Consider the following set:\n\n$$\nA={1,3}\n$$\n\nGiven the relation $R$ on $A$ defined by\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x=y,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $1\\,R\\,1$\n- **II.** $1\\,R\\,3$\n- **III.** $3\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,3$" :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆{A}^{2}\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x=y.$ For this relation, note that\n\n- the symbols $R$ and $=$ are interchangeable, and\n\n- the symbols $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ and $\\ne $ are also interchangeable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is  true. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $=$, we have $1=1,$ which is true.\n\n- Statement II is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $=,$ we have $1=3,$ which is false.\n\n- Statement III is false. Replacing $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ with the symbol $\\ne ,$ we have $3\\ne 3,$ which is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411416 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8479a60b-b5db-5ad4-8100-fd2db8002091" :knowledge-point/title "Using the x R y Notation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050648 :topic/id #uuid "5c32a7e5-b594-532c-868b-817b3d0ee933" :topic/math-academy-id 2817 :topic/title "Relations on Finite Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5be660f9-b1a6-5c44-a236-1528e3ac5e2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453706} {:answer/id #uuid "633efbab-1e9c-519d-8c87-cf31633aa603" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5be660f9-b1a6-5c44-a236-1528e3ac5e2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453706} :answer-field/id #uuid "efb6a831-307e-5cc1-8685-62da4be3c7f2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454603} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fe94c89-0c24-5c68-b631-7696e034ff88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453708} {:answer/id #uuid "f9b2dd14-66fb-53c2-8cc1-84b717d05aae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453709}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9b2dd14-66fb-53c2-8cc1-84b717d05aae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453709} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8465c33-c520-5083-bc54-d81a74f17a81" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454604} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f47a411-e333-573c-987e-13415220e695" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453710} {:answer/id #uuid "17e30408-772b-5358-b7a6-03830f24a9aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17e30408-772b-5358-b7a6-03830f24a9aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453711} :answer-field/id #uuid "b62f52a8-c0a4-55c9-8e09-ccce1ff6f34f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454605}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "77fae439-40b7-5f50-94ed-61df5583b377" :question/math-academy-id "q-213144" :question/problem "Consider the following set:\n\n$$\nA={2,4,6}\n$$\n\nGiven the relation $R$ on $A$ defined by\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x∤y,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $2\\,R\\,4$\n- **II.** $4\\,R\\,6$\n- **III.** $2\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,6$" :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆{A}^{2}\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x∤y.$ For this relation, note that\n\n- the symbols $R$ and $∤$ are interchangeable, and\n\n- the symbols $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ and $∣$ are also interchangeable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $∤$, we have $2∤4,$ which is false.\n\n- Statement II is true. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $∤,$ we have $4∤6,$ which is true.\n\n- Statement III is true. Replacing $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ with the symbol $∣,$ we have $2∣6,$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411420 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157236 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f77177ee-74b0-5681-92a8-ed6994ab9f9c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements of Standard Relations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050648 :topic/id #uuid "5c32a7e5-b594-532c-868b-817b3d0ee933" :topic/math-academy-id 2817 :topic/title "Relations on Finite Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "858d1b5f-5918-5ac9-99e7-cf79a2a46733" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472868} {:answer/id #uuid "2533356f-13ee-5d42-ad0e-d1a267e0303d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "858d1b5f-5918-5ac9-99e7-cf79a2a46733" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472868} :answer-field/id #uuid "89cfb84f-7bdd-58d3-bfb5-bb04de54defe" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473829} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e26b1ad-a11f-58c2-b68b-eb2904daa308" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472870} {:answer/id #uuid "904056bb-a15e-552e-9d05-d3e6998208bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "904056bb-a15e-552e-9d05-d3e6998208bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472871} :answer-field/id #uuid "876dfd72-f2f4-50c0-a2d6-2e6b60c3e021" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473830} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "989df4ea-589f-56da-b83c-762f6d608713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472872} {:answer/id #uuid "7477b5ed-7893-5893-8195-ef07b8905aa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "989df4ea-589f-56da-b83c-762f6d608713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472872} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a92b2f8-77ee-5489-93de-bf8f95ddbcef" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473831}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bb1a702e-c18f-5fe7-b6f2-5f1506bc9396" :question/math-academy-id "q-213003" :question/problem "Consider the following set:\n\n$$\nA={{0},{1,0}}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following ordered pairs is an element of the relation \"is **not** a subset of\" on $A?$ \n- **I.** $({0},{1,0})$\n- **II.** $({1,0},{0})$\n- **III.** $({1,0},{1,0})$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆{A}^{2}\n$$\n\nIn this case, $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in {A}^{2}$ such that $x⊈y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our ordered pairs in turn.\n\n- The ordered pair $({0},{1,0})$ is **not** an element of $R$ since ${0}⊆{1,0}.\\,\\times $\n\n- The ordered pair $({1,0},{0})$ is an element of $R$ since ${1,0}⊈{0}.\\,✓$\n\n- The ordered pair $({1,0},{1,0})$ is **not** an element of $R$ since ${1,0}⊆{1,0}.\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411423 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8479a60b-b5db-5ad4-8100-fd2db8002091" :knowledge-point/title "Using the x R y Notation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050648 :topic/id #uuid "5c32a7e5-b594-532c-868b-817b3d0ee933" :topic/math-academy-id 2817 :topic/title "Relations on Finite Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35885383-bf11-52c5-ba9d-4f4b1185ebb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453712} {:answer/id #uuid "3f1f43dd-5919-53ae-a648-3a99f59c4a22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f1f43dd-5919-53ae-a648-3a99f59c4a22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453713} :answer-field/id #uuid "20de8fe4-991c-5757-87fe-b795e35d4479" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454606} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8f51057-de81-5138-a23d-33ea78923c97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453714} {:answer/id #uuid "00dd75c6-eea2-5a86-bfe5-3fdbc213e543" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00dd75c6-eea2-5a86-bfe5-3fdbc213e543" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453715} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e28ba17-46e7-5a69-aeb0-17ccae0ab090" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454607} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d922689-7ef7-5604-8706-8851f69b6923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453716} {:answer/id #uuid "f5fc08b8-39cf-571a-8ab5-29a1d31aa564" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453717}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d922689-7ef7-5604-8706-8851f69b6923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453716} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7423bc3-695e-500a-99f4-aadd8e9ace7b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454608}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e3479154-8b81-59b7-8f1a-b3765342f61c" :question/math-academy-id "q-213145" :question/problem "Consider the following set:\n\n$$\nA={1,2}\n$$\n\nGiven the relation $R$ on $A$ defined by\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x∣y,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $1\\,R\\,1$\n- **II.** $1\\,R\\,2$\n- **III.** $2\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,2$" :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆{A}^{2}\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x∣y.$ For this relation, note that\n\n- the symbols $R$ and $∣$ are interchangeable, and\n\n- the symbols $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ and $∤$ are also interchangeable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $∣$, we have $1∣1,$ which is true.\n\n- Statement II is true. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $∣,$ we have $1∣2,$ which is true.\n\n- Statement III is false. Replacing $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ with the symbol $∤,$ we have $2∤2,$ which is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411427 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8479a60b-b5db-5ad4-8100-fd2db8002091" :knowledge-point/title "Using the x R y Notation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050648 :topic/id #uuid "5c32a7e5-b594-532c-868b-817b3d0ee933" :topic/math-academy-id 2817 :topic/title "Relations on Finite Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "062ff4a9-f6fb-5801-b6eb-0952304ea02b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453676} {:answer/id #uuid "339f6035-7726-57fe-9feb-d831cfd2e14c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "062ff4a9-f