er/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473468} {:answer/id #uuid "44d28dcb-0256-5a04-865b-984aeab7ba22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44d28dcb-0256-5a04-865b-984aeab7ba22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473469} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd426fda-1266-52bf-9a5b-ad1aacb1c6ed" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474129}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "46c22425-ee4e-5a56-9d8f-8f1ffa9ada86" :question/math-academy-id "q-84748" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables could be modeled as a binomial distribution?\n- **I.** The ages of $20$ soccer players\n- **II.** The price of a pair of pants in a department store\n- **III.** The number of wins by a basketball team in a $30$-game season if the probability of the team winning any individual game is $55%$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A binomial distribution models the number of successes in a sequence of $n$ independent experiments (where each outcome is either success or failure).\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable I could *not* be modeled as a binomial distribution. The ages cannot be interpreted as \"success\" or \"failure.\"\n\n- Random variable II could *not* be modeled as a binomial distribution. The prices cannot be interpreted as \"success\" or \"failure.\"\n\n- Random variable III could be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of wins in $30$ games can be interpreted as the number of successes in a sequence of $30$ independent experiments.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411567 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105827 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "162690db-70b3-54a8-a920-576a484a42d9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Random Variables that Follow a Binomial Distribution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049632 :topic/id #uuid "06f86dee-da2a-593c-8633-10b2e3189b5c" :topic/math-academy-id 1395 :topic/title "Modeling With the Binomial Distribution"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10e3af4b-f9ce-5ba6-b0a6-1cd12c611ba0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473458} {:answer/id #uuid "6f111d65-5eb1-5e5e-ab6d-178cdb7b3a90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f111d65-5eb1-5e5e-ab6d-178cdb7b3a90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473459} :answer-field/id #uuid "55b6a24c-c00a-580c-9242-b3b1d2c15eb6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474124} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "115a22bb-c84b-5724-b6ef-88afb26dba89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473460} {:answer/id #uuid "7f635d5f-9325-57a9-92db-9b9f4c6e34fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "115a22bb-c84b-5724-b6ef-88afb26dba89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473460} :answer-field/id #uuid "746cd9ee-265d-573a-9065-80f853b84b0d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 