Pq=q$\n- **III.** $q$ is a steady-state vector of $P$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $q$ such that $Pq=q.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $q$ is a stochastic vector since its entries are non-negative and add up to $1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Note that\n\n$$\nPq=\\begin{bmatrix}0.3 & 0.8 \\\\ 0.7 & 0.2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0.1 \\\\ 0.9\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0.03+0.72 \\\\ 0.07+0.18\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0.75 \\\\ 0.25\\end{bmatrix}\\ne q.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $Pq\\ne q,$ it is not a steady-state vector of $P.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048393 :topic/id #uuid "9babae1d-ca0d-5438-a2e4-a65dbba9f7ef" :topic/math-academy-id 1913 :topic/title "Steady-State Vectors"} :activity/title "Steady-State Vectors" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411596} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411620}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411677 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203899 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff71f3f5-8383-5815-ba42-289f14e16b57" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Ordered Pairs Belonging to a Standard Relation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050176 :topic/id #uuid "340a9570-0274-5535-83f9-7912961ba2ff" :topic/math-academy-id 4826 :topic/title "Relations on Infinite Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7252f882-e1d0-5f4c-97ae-178f26c429a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453682} {:answer/id #uuid "c4e6f041-b9c8-5dec-9c77-5d180a2045a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :an