86045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473390} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a38ae81-8d40-5e8f-ad84-7cf8d41e0b85" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474090}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "abd84654-ac2d-58a6-9574-529f2b4aa6f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-78597" :question/problem "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[-7]_{11}?$\n\nI. $15$\n\nII. $-4$\n\nIII. $7$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The residue class $[-7]_{11}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $-7$ modulo $11.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[-7]_{11} & =\\{x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡-7\\,(\\text{mod}\\,11)\\} \\\\  & =\\{x\\in Z\\,|\\,x=-7+11k,\\,k\\in Z\\} \\\\  & =\\{-7+11k\\,|\\,k\\in Z\\} \\\\  & =\\{…,\\,-7-2\\cdot 11,\\,-7-11,\\,-7,\\,-7+11,\\,-7+2\\cdot 11,\\,…\\} \\\\  & =\\{…,-29,-18,-7,4,15,…\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $15$ belongs to $[-7]_{11},$ while $-4$ and $7$ do not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412975 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152098 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c1fe7ea-d91e-5440-b756-37a460a18f19" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Residue Classes Containing a Given Element" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050597 :topic/id #uuid "574a92ea-12bd-55d4-a248-945298d922a1" :topic/math-academy-id 2655 :topic/title "Residue Classes"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "755751ed-eb2f-5baa-977d-50e0cf4d1cab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473494} {:answer/id #uuid "f84e8c37-3c47-5019-bbd8-6aba66d56fe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :