ield/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454551}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1261accc-9253-5b2b-9450-d1cf9dd3a558" :question/math-academy-id "q-181624" :question/problem "$$\nX=\\{a,b,2,4\\},\\,Y=\\{n\\in N∣\\,1\\le n<5\\}\n$$\n\nConsider the sets $X$ and $Y$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $|X|=4$\n\n- **II.** $|Y|=5$\n\n- **III.** $|X|=|Y|$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that finite sets have the same cardinality if and only if they have the same number of elements.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $X$ is a finite set and $|X|=4.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that $Y=\\{1,2,3,4\\}$ is a finite set and $|Y|=4.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, $X$ and $Y$ are finite sets and  $|X|=|Y|=4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414421 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171919 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "308a8c68-628a-522f-9545-17a7165aefdf" :knowledge-point/title "Finite Vs. Infinite Sets" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050146 :topic/id #uuid "30c306d4-7422-557a-a542-cedff2b28c58" :topic/math-academy-id 3424 :topic/title "Discrete Infinite Sets With Equal Cardinality"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4a6a196-cf6f-52f0-8045-af9ff9cb5144" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453604} {:answer/id #uuid "742d1d8a-016b-5906-b5da-c25348b65e17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "742d1d8a-016b-5906-b5da-c25348b65e17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident 