uuid "4c2743b2-72ab-5576-b421-aa5dcedd6c11" :question/math-academy-id "q-181626" :question/problem "$$\nS=\\{1,1,2,3,\\{4,5\\}\\},\\,T=\\{n\\in N∣\\,2\\le n\\le 7\\}\n$$\n\nConsider the sets $S$ and $T$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $|S|=4$\n\n- **II.** $|T|=5$\n\n- **III.** $|S|=|T|$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that finite sets have the same cardinality if and only if they have the same number of elements.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed,  $S$ is a finite set and $|S|=4.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that $T=\\{2,3,4,5,6,7\\}$ is a finite set and $|T|=6.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $4\\ne 6,$ we conclude that $|S|\\ne |T|.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414495 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124477 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "488c9762-554b-5ea6-b414-ce6cbde9bbd1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049723 :topic/id #uuid "0e15397e-6c32-508c-b6ea-90f1a9e5a237" :topic/math-academy-id 1904 :topic/title "Identifying the Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "293dfe13-f59f-562c-a0be-1139ae738cb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574359} {:answer/id #uuid "3ceede24-68c2-5b95-a0ae-f71371a3af85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ceede24-68c2-5b95-a0ae-f71371a3af85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574360} :answer-field/id #uuid "234f0e71-dc12-5b4d-957f-0aa1ca60edfc" :answer-field/key "Column 1" :answer-field/type {: