dent :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574487 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186574064 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414497} :task-item/status {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571}}]} :answer-field/id #uuid "36122477-3b36-52c8-9e0e-342500a14c0a" :answer-field/key "Column 4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574726}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ef768962-c254-565f-ad90-7c7187cd37b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-73613" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $2$nd column." :task-item/_content [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186574064 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414497} :task-item/elapsed-seconds 29.044 :task-item/id #uuid "fbe62d87-634f-4748-8f2b-57c4ba4bfd6c" :task-item/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186574065} :task-item/responses [{:answer/id #uuid "07dd3a62-9196-5860-8cf0-54167b0a8664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574481} {:answer/id #uuid "8c7bca81-a7c3-57cd-99dd-b5286cc40d82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574484} {:answer/id #uuid "fb638359-5c89-5d36-81ac-4c070d3f5081" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/