th-academy-id "q-213394" :question/problem "Given that $10a≡10b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4),$ which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$\n\n- **II.** $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)$\n\n- **III.** $9a≡9b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)$" :question/worked-solution "The division properties of modular arithmetic state the following:\n\n- For $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\n- For $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=1,$ we have \n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. Applying the first property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10a & ≡10b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,4) \\\\ 2\\cdot 5\\cdot a & ≡2\\cdot 5\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2\\cdot 2) \\\\ \\cancel{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{2}\\cdot 5) \\\\ 5a & ≡5b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $gcd(5,2)=1,$ by the second property, we have:\n\n$$\n5a≡5b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. By statement II and the second property, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)\\,⟺\\,9a≡9b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415047 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152094 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bca70f6c-d087-5b8e-aff2-581adca9ed1f" :knowledge-point/title "Using the First Division Property" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050689 :topic/id #uuid "5f54d743-67b1-5023-a4c2-42de103b3b6d" :topic/math-academy-id 2675 :topic/title "The Division Properties of Modular Arithmetic"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "215a3373-c92b-5c76-a4aa-8454ff12465a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answ