 :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472896} {:answer/id #uuid "cc4aa1c2-d50b-5650-b4a2-854650814eb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc4aa1c2-d50b-5650-b4a2-854650814eb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472897} :answer-field/id #uuid "a38545ae-c736-5805-8a9e-09fed758aff1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e27df10f-2205-5c33-84a9-013636e28935" :question/math-academy-id "q-213167" :question/problem "![](images/35/35756183a7b4bf08baffb00d1f35dcc370b0e58831554daafa58d8f3d4359ab6.png)\n\nThe plot of the binary relation $S,$ defined over the set $X=\\{2,4,6\\}$ is given above. Which of the following ordered pairs belong to the relation?\n\nI. $(2,2)$\n\nII. $(4,4)$\n\nIII. $(6,2)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A binary relation can be visualized using a plot (or graph), where \n\n- the first set is plotted along the horizontal axis,\n\n- the second set is plotted along the vertical axis, and\n\n- each pair $(x,y)$ from the relation defines a point with coordinates $(x,y)$ on the plot.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given ordered pairs.\n\n- The pair $(2,2)$ belongs to the relation. Indeed, the plot contains a point with these coordinates.\n\n- The pair $(4,4)$ does not belong to the relation since the plot does not contain a point with such coordinates.\n\n- The pair $(6,2)$ belongs to the relation. Indeed, the plot contains a point with these coordinates.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416481 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184197 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8063bc9c-a10d-562b-93b1-508b4b26a674" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Singular Values of a Matrix" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049462 :topic/id #uuid "f7488799-2322-5ff9-8065-6852954f5eb5" :topic/math-academy-id 3819 :topic/title "Computing the Singular Values of a Matrix"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc84e201-9a3b-5b9c-b271-053b83bc1062" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454190} {:answer/id #uuid "b48f37d9-b3b3-5755-8843-513b5d12ef8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc84e201-9a3b-5b9c-b271-053b83bc1062" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454190} :answer-field/id #uuid "13a9bc41-dd9b-55b8-81b0-283e2528d477" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454845} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52687df0-1468-50e5-b467-bf1e68ad8627" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454192} {:answer/id #uuid "47e41440-ce24-5373-9725-7970eff71e7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52687df0-1468-50e5-b467-bf1e68ad8627" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454192} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff9c9bed-0a04-5ac5-9daa-956eebe2c80a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454846} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "339ff9c4-e5b0-5f71-b0a6-e74576728ce2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454194} {:answer/id #uuid "57d27c03-79c7-5bcb-8497-d684476d3e9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57d27c03-79c7-5bcb-8497-d684476d3e9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454195} :answer-field/id #uuid "179dae7d-b2f1-55f0-bd24-81b68af5b4fa" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454847}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5650e0d2-585c-5516-892d-5eacef061cb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-95266" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** Any $2\\times 3$ matrix $A$ has at most $2$ distinct singular values.\n- **II.** The matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$ has one negative singular value.\n- **III.** Any $5\\times 3$ matrix $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values." :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $3\\times 3$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{3\\times 2}\\times {A}_{2\\times 3}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{3\\times 3}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement II is false. All singular values of any matrix are non-negative. So, $A$ can't have a negative singular value.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ is a $5\\times 3$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $3\\times 5$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $3\\times 3$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{3\\times 5}\\times {A}_{5\\times 3}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{3\\times 3}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416485 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184197 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8063bc9c-a10d-562b-93b1-508b4b26a674" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Singular Values of a Matrix" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049462 :topic/id #uuid "f7488799-2322-5ff9-8065-6852954f5eb5" :topic/math-academy-id 3819 :topic/title "Computing the Singular Values of a Matrix"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4129371-905f-54bf-ae87-c438b2fd43aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454184} {:answer/id #uuid "77bf2baa-cff5-52ce-8b41-e36aedb6e4a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77bf2baa-cff5-52ce-8b41-e36aedb6e4a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454185} :answer-field/id #uuid "861de6d8-648e-5127-85e8-5f06c2f6e1e5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454842} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4731f9ee-31e7-5b9b-a569-ce496f29e4a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454186} {:answer/id #uuid "2b6665d1-709e-5474-aae8-a9d99f2ffbe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b6665d1-709e-5474-aae8-a9d99f2ffbe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454187} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5399265-62f4-5593-8a3d-8303b79fd15a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454843} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03d6caf3-6217-5f02-8760-2707cabb06a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454188} {:answer/id #uuid "7e82bf64-150d-5e41-acc3-db5ca4cb19c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03d6caf3-6217-5f02-8760-2707cabb06a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454188} :answer-field/id #uuid "416af97e-bb3e-58d1-b299-f595bb03d963" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454844}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e69dd032-aa5c-5891-a7fc-97b84703e88a" :question/math-academy-id "q-95261" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** Any $4\\times 3$ matrix $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n- **II.** The singular values of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}$ are non-negative.\n- **III.** Any $3\\times 4$ matrix $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values." :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $A$ is a $4\\times 3$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $3\\times 3$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{3\\times 4}\\times {A}_{4\\times 3}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{3\\times 3}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement II is true. All singular values of any matrix are non-negative.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $4\\times 3$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $4\\times 4$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{4\\times 3}\\times {A}_{3\\times 4}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{4\\times 4}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $4$ distinct singular values.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416486 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184197 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8063bc9c-a10d-562b-93b1-508b4b26a674" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Singular Values of a Matrix" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049462 :topic/id #uuid "f7488799-2322-5ff9-8065-6852954f5eb5" :topic/math-academy-id 3819 :topic/title "Computing the Singular Values of a Matrix"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17199cb6-adea-5b61-919d-b8c404e0acce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454196} {:answer/id #uuid "8d2c651a-9fde-5d68-8dc6-db31d39c222f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d2c651a-9fde-5d68-8dc6-db31d39c222f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454197} :answer-field/id #uuid "4075aa54-0dff-530d-8aaa-0316bbe68384" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454848} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ecfe78bb-58cf-5df3-9fec-25b0e56a5cf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454198} {:answer/id #uuid "1cdaafa5-1a83-54e7-855b-cedee6333689" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ecfe78bb-58cf-5df3-9fec-25b0e56a5cf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454198} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebe209e3-0b27-5e04-917c-a2a111895c0f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454849} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72750c08-7405-534f-a4d7-2b63080f7417" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454200} {:answer/id #uuid "cf58434d-bb62-5004-8244-73fdeaf3e6f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72750c08-7405-534f-a4d7-2b63080f7417" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454200} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b11c932-8a01-5b51-9317-14a5c84895c3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454850}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fef86daf-091a-52fa-bcf0-1d2b609bb348" :question/math-academy-id "q-95281" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** Any $6\\times 3$ matrix $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n- **II.** The matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$ has one negative singular value.\n- **III.** Any $4\\times 5$ matrix $A$ has at most $4$ distinct singular values." :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since $A$ is a $6\\times 3$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $3\\times 6$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $3\\times 3$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{3\\times 6}\\times {A}_{6\\times 3}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{3\\times 3}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement II is false. All singular values of any matrix are non-negative. So, $A$ can't have a negative singular value.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is a $4\\times 5$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $5\\times 4$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $5\\times 5$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{5\\times 4}\\times {A}_{4\\times 5}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{5\\times 5}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $5$ distinct singular values.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049462 :topic/id #uuid "f7488799-2322-5ff9-8065-6852954f5eb5" :topic/math-academy-id 3819 :topic/title "Computing the Singular Values of a Matrix"} :activity/title "Computing the Singular Values of a Matrix" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507599} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508139}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416857 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203923 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "306be17f-f950-57e2-9cb7-2b33c8a4929e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations Over Infinite Sets" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048805 :topic/id #uuid "c10b84fd-2e2a-576b-a2ce-4b2fb0bbd333" :topic/math-academy-id 4820 :topic/title "Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54b51a22-f7bb-516c-8946-37f7bb536744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472910} {:answer/id #uuid "7e001c66-2d5e-5fc7-9dbc-75651f93ff2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472911}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54b51a22-f7bb-516c-8946-37f7bb536744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472910} :answer-field/id #uuid "913db174-dca4-594b-9349-a0c1ec9bdf75" :answer-field/key "R" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473850} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb56dc5f-3259-5b31-bf7c-98631cb8f596" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472912} {:answer/id #uuid "8007d323-54e1-5ead-962c-cf2ea1cafe75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472913}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8007d323-54e1-5ead-962c-cf2ea1cafe75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472913} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0f55f7c-bbee-5d76-9c4b-0e605262a0f8" :answer-field/key "S" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473851} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc35629f-7217-578b-9b12-67f715419ec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472914} {:answer/id #uuid "729c04b6-1d28-5013-bdf4-e11e5a5716c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc35629f-7217-578b-9b12-67f715419ec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472914} :answer-field/id #uuid "304f4a81-f362-5264-ba0f-bf630eeb8f19" :answer-field/key "T" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473852}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "653fba49-a6b9-5e57-b514-cf99f2424cd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-213246" :question/problem "Which of the following relations are reflexive?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **R.** $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x≡2y\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7),$ defined on $Z$\n\n- **S.** $x\\,S\\,y$ if and only if $x≡y\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9),$ defined on $Z$\n\n- **T.** $x\\,T\\,y$ if and only if $y≡x+2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6),$ defined on $Z$" :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our relations.\n\n- Relation $R$ is neither reflexive nor irreflexive. Notice that \n\n- $(1,1)\\notin R$ since $1≢2(1)\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7),$ while\n\n- $(7,7)\\in R$ since $7≡2(7)\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7).$\n\n- Relation $S$ is reflexive. Indeed, $(x,x)\\in S$ for all $x\\in Z.$ Notice that \n\n$$\nx≡x\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)\n$$\n\nfor any $x\\in Z.$\n\n- Relation $T$ is irreflexive. Indeed, $(x,x)\\notin T$ for all $x\\in Z.$ Notice that \n\n$$\nx≢x+2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)\n$$\n\nfor any $x\\in Z.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$S$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416858 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203923 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "306be17f-f950-57e2-9cb7-2b33c8a4929e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations Over Infinite Sets" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048805 :topic/id #uuid "c10b84fd-2e2a-576b-a2ce-4b2fb0bbd333" :topic/math-academy-id 4820 :topic/title "Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c5e9fa8-fe85-584f-9357-ebf63d048548" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472904} {:answer/id #uuid "66b4445c-dbcb-5102-9c36-f0a58c26a8dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c5e9fa8-fe85-584f-9357-ebf63d048548" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472904} :answer-field/id #uuid "47d00bf4-25af-50a2-a5c7-60cf25635139" :answer-field/key "R" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473847} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7693ccf5-ebef-506c-9ea0-9937ffdc087d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472906} {:answer/id #uuid "701be496-842e-571f-bace-1e77be1e0583" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "701be496-842e-571f-bace-1e77be1e0583" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472907} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2c7a48d-a097-5db1-8647-b1c560da077b" :answer-field/key "S" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473848} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd1fefe6-97a4-519e-b49e-cd175d9f6343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472908} {:answer/id #uuid "fe0313a3-8030-57e9-8c51-ecd36a905e62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd1fefe6-97a4-519e-b49e-cd175d9f6343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472908} :answer-field/id #uuid "c942da9b-3098-5e2c-bc69-59eb0d35646e" :answer-field/key "T" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473849}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7095468b-6aec-5ce6-83d1-ea12403a6b5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-213240" :question/problem "Which of the following relations are reflexive?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **R.** $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x+y)∣10,$ defined on $Z$\n\n- **S.** $x\\,S\\,y$ if and only if $4∣({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}),$ defined on $Z$\n\n- **T.** $x\\,T\\,y$ if and only if $x∣(y+1),$ defined on $Z$" :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our relations.\n\n- Relation $R$ is neither reflexive nor irreflexive. Notice that \n\n- $(2,2)\\notin R$ since $2+2=4$ and $4∤10,$ while\n\n- $(1,1)\\in R$ since $1+1=2$ and $2∣10.$\n\n- Relation $S$ is reflexive. Indeed, $(x,x)\\in S$ for all $x\\in Z.$ Notice that \n\n$$\n4∣({x}^{2}-{x}^{2})\n$$\n\nfor any $x\\in Z.$\n\n- Relation $T$ is neither reflexive nor irreflexive. Notice that \n\n- $(2,2)\\notin T$ since $2∤(2+1),$ while\n\n- $(1,1)\\in T$ since $1∣(1+1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$S$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416863 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203922 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4b47a31-7bda-5366-bac4-1d070776e776" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations From a Diagram" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048805 :topic/id #uuid "c10b84fd-2e2a-576b-a2ce-4b2fb0bbd333" :topic/math-academy-id 4820 :topic/title "Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a29f9cbb-000d-5b8c-9f6c-2b45ca8f9c9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472898} {:answer/id #uuid "bb936d2a-d218-5632-94f0-f74248519d79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb936d2a-d218-5632-94f0-f74248519d79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472899} :answer-field/id #uuid "61b2f428-c732-5a03-845e-71d541cb66c5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473844} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e88f6e62-a168-5578-bc6f-cde1ddbb2379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472900} {:answer/id #uuid "01a0001b-a449-59f4-9d85-6090aa040780" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e88f6e62-a168-5578-bc6f-cde1ddbb2379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472900} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1cb8e60-7f3f-5cab-a5a8-f9261791e5bd" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473845} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cff02f99-4992-5465-bf2c-8b903daf43f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472902} {:answer/id #uuid "3b6fc2e4-b2f4-5892-9fc2-d6d8f7bc0bfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b6fc2e4-b2f4-5892-9fc2-d6d8f7bc0bfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472903} :answer-field/id #uuid "af3b864c-298a-50d4-be87-b47b4870ee67" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e1a27c07-b36b-5525-ba6b-847b13ebf516" :question/math-academy-id "q-213228" :question/problem "![](images/03/03ddf06402ad38708d232cf28783c817bf881965d54650eb158e7ffca4ea76a2.png)\n\nWhich of the plots above represent irreflexive relations defined on the set $A=\\{1,2,3\\}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nSince $R$ must be irreflexive, we require \n\n$$\n(1,1)\\notin R,\\,(2,2)\\notin R,\\,(3,3)\\notin R.\n$$\n\nThese ordered pairs correspond to the diagonal points on the plots, as shown below:\n\n![](images/b6/b63d99459e8271e70ec36fd417d67565f3d5e77316815d49c235468e174aa1e9.png)\n\n \n\nA plot corresponding to an irreflexive relation must not contain diagonal points. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416924 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd3fd748-f238-59b2-badf-54b6e762836c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Statistics" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049367 :topic/id #uuid "ef34739b-f46e-5073-bcb9-1acc5022fae9" :topic/math-academy-id 3864 :topic/title "Sampling Distributions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aa80fb6-08ad-5ab5-9b84-28cc06a2687a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472712} {:answer/id #uuid "e3efc5a3-366a-5a29-a48e-d8ddbd406cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3efc5a3-366a-5a29-a48e-d8ddbd406cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472713} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5f52a81-37f3-5813-b236-8991da4825e6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473751} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f833641-c372-57ac-ba60-2d4f8e69063b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472714} {:answer/id #uuid "0c7b19d5-5886-5396-88bc-bf5f4bbca3db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c7b19d5-5886-5396-88bc-bf5f4bbca3db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472715} :answer-field/id #uuid "e28af8a5-3e58-5224-82c5-28d1a62a2d64" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473752} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb2a9643-7098-501a-9ebc-7cfb1fab4258" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472716} {:answer/id #uuid "60b54385-bc72-5ca7-92b5-e42793fb3038" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472717}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb2a9643-7098-501a-9ebc-7cfb1fab4258" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472716} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1fe5d17-2a3a-5760-88f2-5077ef1873c0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473753}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "062c6773-1c0f-5106-b2b7-7c444f43389f" :question/math-academy-id "q-139820" :question/problem "A sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{15}$ is drawn from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population standard deviation $\\sigma .$ If $\\mu $ and $\\sigma $ are both unknown, which of the following are statistics?\n\nI. ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}|{X}_{i}|$\n\nII. $min({X}_{1},{X}_{3},…,{X}_{13},{X}_{15})$\n\nIII. $max({X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{15},\\sigma )$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population. A statistic is a random variable expressed as a function of ${X}_{i}.$\n\nStatistics cannot involve unknown population parameters.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each expression. \n\n- Expression I is a statistic. It is a function of the sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{15}$ only.\n\n- Expression II is also a statistic. It is a function of the sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{15}$ only. Note that a statistic doesn't need to include every sample element.\n\n- Expression III is *not* a statistic. It is a function that contains the unknown population standard deviation $\\sigma .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416927 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd3fd748-f238-59b2-badf-54b6e762836c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Statistics" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049367 :topic/id #uuid "ef34739b-f46e-5073-bcb9-1acc5022fae9" :topic/math-academy-id 3864 :topic/title "Sampling Distributions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91928ab5-1c08-5709-ade9-42c3fbbc3f62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472736} {:answer/id #uuid "8ee1a951-eaaf-5f12-8f31-8f125d603255" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472737}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91928ab5-1c08-5709-ade9-42c3fbbc3f62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472736} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f5bc247-9c01-53e3-aadd-ed34804268a7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473763} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d5702a5-502e-5b8d-9267-895c288c6f32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472738} {:answer/id #uuid "af515352-e650-5ec1-92cb-48d3ce1f3514" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d5702a5-502e-5b8d-9267-895c288c6f32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472738} :answer-field/id #uuid "81ff48ec-fbac-56c6-88aa-5530077f7640" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473764} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f929db08-b244-5145-89ee-3131d2530bfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472740} {:answer/id #uuid "df817a80-9731-505c-9947-3f51347deb8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df817a80-9731-505c-9947-3f51347deb8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472741} :answer-field/id #uuid "b551a732-145c-5747-b844-8f4d584df8bc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473765}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4893e2e1-c5c0-525e-90bd-45f0ee89d95b" :question/math-academy-id "q-143552" :question/problem "A sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{16}$ is drawn from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}.$ If $\\mu $ is unknown and $\\sigma $ is known, which of the following are statistics?\n- **I.** $\\mu \\cdot \\sigma -\\text{min}({X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{16})$\n- **II.** $\\mu -\\text{median}({X}_{2},{X}_{4},…,{X}_{16})$\n- **III.** $\\sigma -max({X}_{1},{X}_{3},…,{X}_{15})$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population. A statistic is a random variable expressed as a function of ${X}_{i}.$\n\nStatistics cannot involve unknown population parameters.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each expression.\n\n- Expressions I and II are *not* statistics. They are functions that contain the unknown population mean $\\mu .$\n\n- Expression III is a statistic. It is a function of the sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{16}$ and the *known* population standard deviation $\\sigma $ only. Note that a statistic doesn't need to include every sample element.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416928 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd3fd748-f238-59b2-badf-54b6e762836c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Statistics" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049367 :topic/id #uuid "ef34739b-f46e-5073-bcb9-1acc5022fae9" :topic/math-academy-id 3864 :topic/title "Sampling Distributions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab934dba-e3a2-5d59-ae83-e95f06179b50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472700} {:answer/id #uuid "8f7b43a7-81e3-5385-a0ab-8aadc7cfbe8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f7b43a7-81e3-5385-a0ab-8aadc7cfbe8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472701} :answer-field/id #uuid "d026cafa-0a30-51b7-99c1-cb46a04536a8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473745} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "063a719d-4200-54